{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When your brother grows poor, etc.</b> This passage alludes to a great matter and a cautionary reminder to the inhabitants of the world. <b>כִּי יָמוּךְ</b> — in the manner of the verse (Ecclesiastes 10:18): ״בַּעֲצַלְתַּיִם יִמַּךְ הַמְּקָרֶה״, and our Sages, whose memory is for blessing, said (Ta'anit 7a): You have done to that One of whom it is said (Psalms 104:3): ״הַמְקָרֶה בַמַּיִם עֲלִיּוֹתָיו״ — מָךְ, for when those below deviate from the good path, the influxes withdraw and the pillar of holiness is weakened, for the essential matter depends on those below." "And He said <b>and sells from his possession.</b> This refers to the Mishkan, the Mishkan of the Testimony, which is His possession, may He be blessed, for in it He caused His Shekhinah to dwell; and through our sins the House was sold into the hand of the nations. As our Sages, whose memory is for blessing, said (Midrash Tehillim 79) in explanation of the verse ״מִזְמוֹר לְאָסָף בָּאוּ גוֹיִם״ etc. And the verse informs us that its redemption lies in the hand of the righteous one who is near to HaShem, in the manner of the verse (Leviticus 10:3): ״בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ״ — he shall redeem his brother's sale. For the Master, blessed is He, calls the righteous ones brother, as it were, as it is written (Psalms 122:8): ״לְמַעַן אַחַי וְרֵעָי״, and the redemption will come about through his stirring the hearts of the children of men, and he says to them: ״Is it good for you that you sit outside, exiled from the table of your Father? And what would be sweet to you about life in the world without the supernal companionship, when you were leaning close around the table of your Father — He is the God of the world, blessed is He forever?״ And he will make despised in their eyes the lusts that merely appear to be, and he will arouse in them a spiritual desire, also felt by every living possessor of a soul, until their deeds improve. And through this HaShem will redeem His sale. And concerning this, all the masters of the earth among the great ones of Israel will be called to give account, and from them HaShem will seek reparation for the affronted House."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:01:23.889404661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}